  "summary": "wormgpt-cli ships a remote-access implant with credential/clipboard stealers and system reconnaissance",
  "details": "The package ships an implant module (src/implant/implant.js) that spawns shells (bash, powershell) and screen-capture processes under child_process control, plus a clipboard stealer (src/implant/stealers/clipboard.js) that invokes powershell via execSync. src/protocol.js constructs POST requests over http/https containing host identifiers and process.env values, and src/tui/app.js reads files from the user's home directory (os.homedir()) and posts them to a remote endpoint. The combination — spawned interactive shells, screen capture, clipboard theft, filesystem reads under the home directory, and process.env plus hostname collection posted to a remote host — is a remote-access trojan / info-stealer shape rather than a benign CLI. The package name openly advertises the WormGPT malware brand and the shipped code matches that stated purpose.",
